 low likelihood due to lack of external trauma signs and self-reported vomiting only", "Alcoholic gastritis with occult bleeding: reduced plausibility due to rectal bleeding (Hematochezia) rather than expected hematemesis/melena from upper GI source"], "alarm_features": ["Recent excessive alcohol intake and vomiting (Mallory-Weiss syndrome context)", "Bright red blood pattern (implying lower GI origin)", "Mild anemia in a previously healthy patient"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Upper Gastrointestinal Bleed (Acute)", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.18939374569579034, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Normal abdominal exam with no obstruction or mass strongly supports ruling out malignancy (B7) and indirectly favors isolated vascular malformation (B2) as the most plausible, localized cause of hematochezia."]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lower Gastrointestinal Vascular Malformation", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.4602268020407707, "danger": 0.3, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Normal abdominal exam with no obstruction or mass strongly supports ruling out malignancy (B7) and indirectly favors isolated vascular malformation (B2) as the most plausible, localized cause of hematochezia."], "evidence_against": ["While Mallory-Weiss syndrome (B1) is an upper GI source, the theoretical possibility of hematochezia due to rapid transit creates weak support for B1 and introduces mild doubt about B2 as the exclusive explanation."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of prior spontaneous GI bleeding", "Location of symptoms (left vs right side)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Colonoscopy", "Angiocontrast imaging of pelvis"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.65, "interrupt_relevance": 0.2, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Acute Infectious/Inflammatory Colonic Process", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.3409087422524226, "danger": 0.4, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B6": {"id": "B6", "label": "Reactive Gastrointestinal Injury", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 1.022726226757268e-06, "danger": 0.2, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B7": {"id": "B7", "label": "Lower Gastrointestinal Neoplasm with Bleeding", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.009469687284789518, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Normal abdominal exam with no obstruction or mass strongly supports ruling out malignancy (B7) and indirectly favors isolated vascular malformation (B2) as the most plausible, localized cause of hematochezia."]}, "B2.1": {"id": "B2.1", "label": "Colonic Angiodysplasia", "parent": "B2", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.2761360812244624, "posterior": 0.2761360812244624, "danger": 0.35, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Location of symptoms (left vs right side)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Colonoscopy (colon-specific)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.1, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}, "B2.2": {"id": "B2.2", "label": "Rectal Vascular Malformation", "parent": "B2", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.1380680406122312, "posterior": 0.1380680406122312, "danger": 0.3, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_r